From 622dc84f90be7fdf265394e9879090cfd3481dd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:22:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tui_gateway: watch signatures and the kanban poll read only
 on change (card J part 2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design t_01a1d563324d7e8e §3 card J (serve change_watcher + notification poller 2.0 -> 0.7% of a core; the
gateway's change_watcher runs the same code). py-spy of hub serve 251687 (120 s @ 40 Hz): change watcher 107
samples (groups 43, sessions 36, skills 27), kanban poll 38 (subscription rows 24).

- tui_gateway/watch_store.py (new): one kept read-only tracked connection per store, keyed on file identity +
  PRAGMA data_version (exact per commit; no racy-mtime window). Bounded LRU (32), dropped on replace, on a missing
  file (forget) and on a transaction a caller left open.
- change_watcher: _db_content_sig (groups) and _session_db_content_sig (sessions) read through it. An unchanged
  store is one PRAGMA; before, every DB/WAL mtime move opened a tracked connection, parsed the schema and closed
  it. The legacy digest throttle keeps its trailing edge (cached key stays stale while held back). Store paths
  resolve once per (dev, ino) instead of an lstat walk per pass.
- skills: published_scopes_signature walks each skill root once per call (memo shared across scopes).
- notification_idle._notify_content: the tui subscription rows (2.1k on the hub, 3 ms) are reused while the
  kanban activity revision covering kanban_notify_subs and the in-flight marks (the one bookkeeping column the
  poll acts on) are unchanged; read in one snapshot with the event scan. Without trigger coverage the rows are
  read on every commit, as before. A chat with a claim in flight is still polled every tick (the due input).
- kanban_activity_revision.covered_revision: public wrapper of the memoised coverage read.

Replay benches (thread_time, hub stream: state.db committed on 92 of 120 passes; main board 92 commits/min,
activity revision 9/min): store signatures 0.075% of a core (base 0.77-0.90%, budget 0.15%); subscription
signature 0.17-0.19% (base 0.63-0.66%, budget 0.3%). RED on base 0fa1a455fd: 7 of 19 new tests.
